+/// `k` for a control matrix B of `n` rows stored as `len` elements. `n` is
+/// non-zero here: `check_dims` runs first. A length that is not a multiple of n
+/// is a `DimensionMismatch` whose expected shape is the smallest whole-column
+/// matrix the slice falls short of.
+fn control_columns(n: usize, len: usize) -> KalmanResult<usize> {
+    match len % n {
+        0 => Ok(len / n),
+        _ => Err(KalmanError::DimensionMismatch { expected: (n, len.div_ceil(n)), actual: (len, 1) }),
+    }
+}
